{
  "id": "HP01Z",
  "version": "2.0",
  "title": "Lymph node biopsy",
  "description": "Lymph node biopsy is removal of a lymph node sample for examination under a microscope. Lymph nodes are part of your immune system, and biopsying them can help diagnose infections, cancers, or other conditions. Your doctor will use imaging to locate the lymph node and remove a sample using either a needle or surgical technique. The sample is sent to a laboratory for analysis to determine the cause of your lymph node enlargement. Results help your doctor diagnose your condition and plan appropriate treatment. Lymph node biopsies can be performed on superficial nodes near your skin or deeper nodes requiring surgical access, depending on which nodes are affected. This type of procedure can be performed various ways, including superficial and open, and the cost may vary depending on the specific approach or service provided.",
